<title>FRANCE: FRENCH ELECTION - Latest projections.</title>
<headline>FRENCH ELECTION - Latest projections.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the latest projections, established at Sunday midnight, by polling institutes after the first round of France's election for the 577-seat National Assembly, held on Sunday.</p>
<p>The first table gives projections for the share of the popular vote in percentages.</p>
<p>The second table gives projections for the number of seats each party or coalition is likely to win after the June 1 runoff.</p>
<p>The projections are based on actual votes counted in sample</p>
<p>constituencies.</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> PROJECTED VOTE		 SOFRES   CSA	  BVA</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme left		    2.4	2.4	 (*)</p>
<p> Communists			9.6     10.5	  9.6</p>
<p> Socialists and allies	28.8     27.9	 28.8</p>
<p> Total left		     40.8     40.8	 38.4</p>
<p> Ecologists			6.4	7	   (*)</p>
<p> Total left + ecologists    47.2     47.8	 38.4</p>
<p> RPR-UDF and allies	   36.5     36	   36.7</p>
<p> National Front		 15.3     15.3	 15.2</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>(*) France 2 gave no BVA estimates for extreme right and</p>
<p>ecologist vote.</p>
<p> PROJECTED SEATS		SOFRES	 CSA	     BVA</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme left		    0		 0	     0</p>
<p> Communists		   21 to 30	19 to 23    17 to 23</p>
<p> Socialists and allies   242 to 272    250 to 275  255 to 280</p>
<p> Total left + ecologists 263 to 302    269 to 298  272 to 303</p>
<p> RPR-UDF and allies	255 to 287    265 to 285  250 to 270</p>
<p> National Front		0 to 3	  0 to 2	0 to 1</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>BVA polls broadcast by France 2 television and Europe 1 radio</p>
<p>SOFRES polls broadcast by TF1 television and RTL radio</p>
<p>CSA polls broadcast by France 3 television and Radio France</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
